{
 "bank": "05",
 "sections": {
  "s05C005": {
   "name": "Scroll sprites: path scroll and inits",
   "summary": [
    "Part of the layer 1/2 scroll sprite system. [$143E]/[$143F] hold the scroll sprite number for layer 1/layer 2; [$1456] = 0 or 4 selects the layer.",
    "Init routines for scroll sprites 0C (Auto-Scroll level), 0D (Fast BG scroll) and 0E (Layer 2 sink/rise), starting at $05C005, $05C01A and $05C036.",
    "$05C04D: auto-scroll along a path of nodes (DATA_05CA6E/05CABE), steps and accelerates layer speed toward the next node.",
    "$05C198: layer 2 variant. $05C283 (scroll sprite 04), $05C32E (0A) and $05C1AE are unused leftover movers.",
    "Per layer L: [$1462+L]/[$1464+L] = X/Y position, [$1446+L]/[$1448+L] = X/Y speed, [$1442+n] = path node, [$1444+n] = segments left."
   ]
  },
  "s05C406": {
   "name": "Table: step and limit values",
   "summary": [
    "Small byte pairs read by CODE_05C4AF: -1/+1 steps, -4/+4 limits, $30/$A0 thresholds."
   ]
  }
 },
